<title>JAPAN: Nansei Sekiyu plans topper turnaround May 1997.</title>
<headline>Nansei Sekiyu plans topper turnaround May 1997.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiner Nansei Sekiyu K.K. said on Thursday it planned to close its 100,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) topper at its Nishihara refinery for about two weeks from May 20, 1997, for maintenance checks.</p>
<p>The Nishihara refinery on Japan's southern island of Okinawa was closed from mid-May to early June this year for maintenance work.</p>
</text>
